# The run says applied. That is Terraform's account of itself.
# These are the same questions asked of AWS instead.

$ aws vpc-lattice list-services              --query 'length(items)'
  0
$ aws vpc-lattice list-service-networks      --query 'length(items)'
  0
$ aws vpc-lattice list-target-groups         --query 'length(items)'
  0

$ aws lambda list-functions \
      --query "length(Functions[?starts_with(FunctionName,'week23')])"
  0
$ aws iam list-roles \
      --query "length(Roles[?starts_with(RoleName,'week23')])"
  0
$ aws ec2 describe-vpcs --filters Name=tag:Name,Values='week23*' \
      --query 'length(Vpcs)'
  0
$ aws logs describe-log-groups \
      --query "length(logGroups[?contains(logGroupName,'week23')])"
  0

# And one question that does not name the week's resources at all,
# in case something was created without the naming convention:

$ aws resourcegroupstaggingapi get-resources --tag-filters Key=Week,Values=23 \
      --query 'length(ResourceTagMappingList)'
  0

The service was the only thing billing by the hour, at $0.025. The VPC
association was free, and stayed free. Nothing here survives to bill again.
